messages:  ['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 226614242 and 631969374? Please reason step by step.\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the sum of 226614242 and 631969374, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Align the numbers by their place values**: This ensures that we are adding the digits in the same place values together. Both numbers have 8 digits, so we can align them vertically:\n\n   ```\n   226614242\n   +631969374\n   ```\n\n2. **Add the digits starting from the rightmost (units place)**: We start by adding the units place digits:\n   - 2 (from 226614242) + 4 (from 631969374) = 6\n\n3. **Move to the next place value (tens place)**: Next, we add the tens place digits:\n   - 4 (from 226614242) + 7 (from 631969374) = 11\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next place value (hundreds place).\n\n4. **Continue adding the digits in the hundreds place**:\n   - 2 (from 226614242) + 9 (from 631969374) + 1 (carried over) = 12\n   - Write down 2 and carry over 1 to the next place value (thousands place).\n\n5. **Add the digits in the thousands place**:\n   - 6 (from 226614242) + 3 (from 631969374) + 1 (carried over) = 10\n   - Write down 0 and carry over 1 to the next place value (ten-thousands place).\n\n6. **Continue adding the digits in the ten-thousands place**:\n   - 1 (from 226614242) + 1 (from 631969374) + 1 (carried over) = 3\n   - Write down 3.\n\n7. **Add the digits in the hundred-thousands place**:\n   - 6 (from 226614242) + 1 (from 631969374) = 7\n   - Write down 7.\n\n8. **Add the digits in the millions place**:\n   - 2 (from 226614242) + 3 (from 631969374) = 5\n   - Write down 5.\n\n9. **Add the digits in the ten-millions place**:\n   - 2 (from 226614242) + 6 (from 631969374) = 8\n   - Write down 8.\n\n10. **Add the digits in the hundred-millions place**:\n    - 0 (from 226614242) + 0 (from 631969374) = 0\n    - Write down 0.\n\nAfter performing all these steps, we get the sum:\n\n```\n  226614242\n+631969374\n---------\n 858583616\n``>\n']
